8:2. **It cannot create learning the fly's connections cannot do.** The diary only re-plays old lessons into the fly's own learning rule. If the fly cannot learn a lesson once, the diary has nothing to keep. In chess this is still unshown: the safe capture stayed below its rival on all three development boards after teaching ([stop report](../../../research/reports/fly-connections-memory-v1-2026-11-07/stop-report-2026-11-09.md)), and the three-board feedback test is still awaiting approval.
18:1. **When memory was put outside the fly, the memory did the thinking.** Memory v8 stored every verified capture and answered new boards with the outcomes of the three most similar stored boards. That is a nearest-neighbour classifier: a method that labels a new item with the labels of the closest stored items ([Cover and Hart 1967](https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1967.1053964)). It judged the moves; the fly only supplied the key. Raw input (383.2) and random features (362.6) beat the fly's key (349.3) with the same store ([v8 report](../../../research/reports/engineered-memory-test-v8-2026-11-07/README.md); `summary.json` reproduced on 2026-11-17: full 349.33, piece-value rule 294.67, all-legal 30.60 against 21.92 for random). In the 2026-11-01 live pilot, the fly's own scores still preferred the old answer after a reversal, and the external store overrode them ([live pilot](../../../research/reports/long-term-memory-v1-live-comparison-2026-11-01/README.md)).
27:1. **Input rule: nothing enters that the fly did not experience.** Every stored field can be rebuilt, byte for byte, from the trial receipts of the fly's own practice: the board it saw, the move it chose, and the teaching pulse it actually received. No certificate, best move, other move's outcome, engine score, test or validation board, or chess rule enters.
28:2. **Output rule: nothing leaves towards a choice.** The memory has no path into move scoring. Its only output is a replayed lesson, delivered through the fly's own eyes and dopamine cells into the fly's own unchanged learning rule.
29:3. **Attribution rule: the fly is tested without the memory.** Every reported score is produced by a process that holds only the fly's connection strengths. The diary is not loaded, and the auditor checks this from the test process's input hashes.
31:Rule 3 is the strongest protection. A memory that is absent at test cannot judge test positions. It can still shape what the fly learns during practice, which is why sections 7 and 8 compare it with matched-practice and memory-only controls.
39:| **Answer lookup store** (v8 line; "episodic control", [Blundell et al. 2016](https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.04460)) | Stores board and outcome; at decision time averages the outcomes of similar stored boards | Yes, if written from receipts | **Yes.** The averaging is a classifier | Separate slots; no overwriting, so it avoids the problem rather than solving it | The similarity measure and the outcome average are the judge | Rejected. Kept as the **memory-only control** |
