53:When a change adds, moves, renames, removes, or repurposes an item covered by a README map or index, update that README and affected links in the **same change**. The person changing the item owns the update. List each major folder in its nearest maintained map with a plain description. Add each new design page and experiment report to its owning index. A new file inside an already indexed experiment only needs a new index link if a reader needs it to understand the report.
83:- **Feedback quality gate:** bind each teaching event to the exact board/history, candidate action, task criterion, independent consequence certificate and its verified scope; record the learner's unaided ranking before feedback. Feedback must explain the verified consequence at the resolution the task supports and identify the responsible earlier choice when sequence credit is claimed. Search estimates and a bare engine score are not verified consequences. Recheck certificates before replay and in the independent audit; reject incomplete, mismatched or resource-exhausted proof as unknown. Report separately the quality of teacher evidence and the limited neural signal actually delivered. Binary valence on a one-ply capture fixture is a narrow mechanism test, not high-quality feedback for multi-ply reasoning. Follow the [feedback quality gate](documentation/design/puzzle-learning/feedback-quality-gate.md).
